---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import AtAGlance from '../../components/AtAGlance.astro';
import InsightCallout from '../../components/InsightCallout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/BeforeAfter.astro';
import FullWidthImage from '../../components/FullWidthImage.astro';

import thumbnail from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/thumbnail.png';
import beforeCaseDetail from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/before-case-detail.png';
import beforeExhibitDetail from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/before-exhibit-detail.png';
import caseListImg from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/case-list.png';
import caseDetailImg from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/case-detail.png';
import exhibitDetailImg from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/exhibit-detail.png';
import mobileViews from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/mobile-views.png';
import addExhibitFlow from '../../assets/images/projects/clearcase/add-exhibit-flow.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="ClearCase"
  description="ClearCase is a fully automated cartridge case triage solution for crime gun investigations. The product worked technically, but it had been built to prove a concept, not to support how investigators work in practice. I led a full UX/UI redesign to fix that, and in the process uncovered a critical gap in the workflow."
  tags={['B2B SaaS', 'UX Audit', 'Responsive Web']}
  heroImage={thumbnail}
  slug="clearcase"
  accentColor="#2c3e50"
  previousProject={{ title: 'Unifying an Investigative Platform', slug: 'unified-platform' }}
  nextProject={{ title: 'GriefShare', slug: 'griefshare' }}
>
  <div class="case-study-body">

    <div class="container">
      <p class="disclaimer">*This work involves sensitive law-enforcement investigations, so I can't share full details publicly. These visuals are representative of the live product, and I'm glad to walk through the complete case study and design decisions in conversation.*</p>
    </div>

    <!-- At a Glance -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="At a Glance" />
        <AtAGlance
          role="Lead Product Designer"
          team="Director of Product (Ballistics), 2 Product Analysts, Director of Software Dev, 1 Senior Engineer, 2 Engineers, 2 QA"
          timeline="5 months, design to launch"
          outcomes={[
            { label: 'New workflow, not just a redesign', text: 'Designed and shipped a web-based exhibit creation flow that didn\'t exist before, allowing lab techs to complete their full workflow on desktop for the first time.' },
            { label: 'Mobile-to-web unlock', text: 'Lab technicians can now manage their entire workflow through the web portal instead of being limited to a mobile app.' },
            { label: 'Live in production', text: 'Full redesign including responsive layout, design system integration, and new exhibit creation flow is shipped and in active use.' },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Challenge -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Challenge"
          subtitle="ClearCase had been ported from mobile to web without rethinking the experience. No design system, no responsive layout, and no real consideration for how investigators actually operate. I started with a comprehensive UX audit before touching any designs, which surfaced deeper workflow gaps that would shape the entire redesign."
        />
        <p class="design-question"><strong>Design Question:</strong> How do you turn a technically capable but workflow-unaware tool into a product investigators actually trust?</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Before -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Before"
          subtitle="The existing web app had sparse layouts, minimal information hierarchy, and required too many clicks to reach key data. Investigators couldn't quickly assess a case or drill into exhibit details without navigating through unnecessary intermediary screens."
        />
        <BeforeAfter
          beforeImage={beforeCaseDetail}
          afterImage={beforeExhibitDetail}
          beforeLabel="Case Detail"
          afterLabel="Exhibit Detail"
          beforeAlt="Original ClearCase case detail page with sparse layout"
          afterAlt="Original ClearCase exhibit detail page requiring extra navigation"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Redesign -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Redesign"
          subtitle="I redesigned every core screen around increased screen real estate and investigator workflows. The case list pairs a searchable, sortable sidebar with a geographic map view. The case detail surfaces the analysis summary, exhibit data, and a downloadable report without extra clicks. And the exhibit detail consolidates photos, metadata, notes, and location into a single view."
        />

        <FullWidthImage
          src={caseListImg}
          alt="Redesigned case list with searchable sidebar and geographic map view"
          caption="Case list: searchable sidebar with map view and case preview on select"
        />

        <div class="image-pair">
          <FullWidthImage
            src={caseDetailImg}
            alt="Redesigned case detail showing analysis summary, firearm table, map, and exhibit cards"
            caption="Case detail: analysis summary, downloadable report, and exhibit views by firearm group"
          />
          <FullWidthImage
            src={exhibitDetailImg}
            alt="Redesigned exhibit detail with photos, metadata, map location, and notes timeline"
            caption="Exhibit detail: photos, metadata, location, and investigation notes in one view"
          />
        </div>

        <FullWidthImage
          src={mobileViews}
          alt="ClearCase responsive mobile views showing case map, exhibit detail, and case detail"
          caption="Fully responsive across devices, built on the LeadsOnline design system"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A Gap Surfaces -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="A Gap Surfaces"
          subtitle="The UX audit flagged it, the redesign made it undeniable, and user feedback confirmed it: the web app had no way to add exhibits. Agencies were hesitant to rely on mobile for core casework, but mobile was the only entry point, leaving investigators at a dead end the moment they needed to act."
        />
        <InsightCallout
          title="Why mobile-only was a non-starter"
          description="Case data stored on a phone, whether personal or work-issued, can be subpoenaed as evidence. Investigators risked losing their device during proceedings, making agencies reluctant to adopt a mobile-only workflow for something as critical as exhibit entry."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Web-Based Exhibit Creation -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Web-Based Exhibit Creation"
          subtitle="In collaboration with engineering, I designed a flow that bridges web and mobile: investigators initiate exhibit creation from the web, scan cartridge cases using the phone's NFC reader via QR code pairing, and the exhibit list updates in real time, all without storing case data on the device. This workflow is now live in production."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={addExhibitFlow}
          alt="End-to-end exhibit creation flow showing web initiation, QR code pairing, mobile NFC scanning, and real-time exhibit list updates"
          caption="The full add-exhibit flow: web initiation, QR pairing, NFC scan on device, real-time sync back to case detail"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Reflection -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="Reflection" />
        <div class="reflections-grid">
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Audit before you redesign</h3>
            <p>Starting with a UX audit before touching the design meant the redesign was grounded in what was actually broken, not just what looked broken. The exhibit creation gap and the buried analysis report both came from that process, not from intuition alone.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>System as accelerator</h3>
            <p>Building on the LeadsOnline design system meant ClearCase felt native to the platform from day one. Shared tokens, components, and patterns cut design time significantly and gave the redesign a coherence it would have taken much longer to achieve from scratch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Know what the product is for</h3>
            <p>ClearCase has a lot of feature potential. The discipline was staying focused on what investigators actually needed: the analysis report and data-rich views that didn't waste their time. Designing for power users means cutting through what's possible to find what's essential.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  .image-pair {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

</style>

<script>
  import { initCaseStudyAnimations } from '../../scripts/scroll-animations';
  import { initScrollVelocityParallax } from '../../scripts/hover-effects';
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    if (!window.location.pathname.startsWith('/projects/clearcase')) return;
    initCaseStudyAnimations('.case-section');
    initScrollVelocityParallax();
  });
</script>
